    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6432": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor and Anatomy and Physiology Coordinator (Non-Tenure Track)",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Assistant Professor and Anatomy and Physiology Coordinator (Non-Tenure Track) Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Assistant Professor and Anatomy and Physiology Coordinator (Non-Tenure Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Position Details Position Overview Position Title Assistant Professor and Anatomy and Physiology Coordinator (Non-Tenure Track) Department 215110 - Biology and Integrated Science, Bus & Tech Appointment Term Non-Tenure Track Position Classification Full-Time, 9 months (Faculty) Grant/Gift Funded (all or a portion)? No If Temporary or Grant Funded, Start Date and End Date Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number FA208PST Position Summary La Salle University’s Natural Sciences Department invites applicants for a full-time, academic year, non-tenure-track faculty position as Anatomy and Physiology coordinator. The position will primarily teach first-year anatomy and physiology courses taken by Nursing majors and health science students. Additionally, the position will serve as the lead for first-year anatomy and physiology courses, ensuring parallel lecture and laboratory sections are consistent, synchronized, and meeting the needs of the degree programs they serve. The successful candidate will provide high-quality instruction in introductory anatomy and physiology while coordinating the first-year Anatomy and Physiology curriculum and teaching efforts. Responsibilities include supporting instructional consistency across lecture and laboratory sections, coordinating with instructors teaching the courses, implementing assessments and course materials, and promoting student success through evidence-based teaching practices. The La Salle University Biology Program fosters a collaborative and interdisciplinary culture dedicated to science undergraduate biology education. We integrate educational best practices and course-based research experiences to train the next generation of nurses, medical practitioners, researchers, and science and health professionals. We seek a dedicated anatomy and physiology instructor with a strong commitment to undergraduate education, excellence in teaching biology at the university-level, and mentoring science students to achieve their full potential to join our team. The position is planned to begin in January at the start of the 2027 spring semester. Essential Duties Teach in an anatomy and physiology (A&P) two-semester course sequence (lecture and lab) that serves primarily first-year nursing and health-sciences majors along with students interested in pursuing medical and health-related careers. Teach related courses as needed by the department. Coordinate other instructors teaching sections of A&P to ensure A&P courses are consistent, synchronized, and meeting the needs of the degree programs these courses serve. Advise on the anatomy and physiology lecture and laboratory curriculum. Coordinate with A&P instructors, the Biology laboratory manager, and department chair to make sure the A&P labs are organized, set up, and meet safety standards. Onboard, train, and support part-time instructors in the A&P program. Maintain, promote, and practice laboratory safety in a laboratory class environment. Secondary Responsibilities Participate in the academic advising for students in the Biology program. Attend Natural Sciences Department faculty meetings. Participate in departmental and university endeavors (such as committees, recruitment events, attend graduation and university events, etc.). Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Biology, Anatomy, Physiology, or a related field. A terminal degree in a field related to human anatomy and physiology (M.D., D.O., D.Pt) will also be considered. Knowledge of and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications A PhD or related terminal degree in a field related to human anatomy and physiology (e.g. M.D., D.O., D.Pt). Experience teaching biology and/or anatomy and physiology courses, particularly at the college-level. Knowledge and experience teaching anatomy and physiology laboratory courses. Ability to collaborate with a team of instructors to ensure consistency and synchronization between different course sections. Demonstrated experience with innovative and effective teaching practices. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Must be able to move around the teaching classroom and laboratory. May involve moving equipment such as anatomy and physiology models. Must be able to work with common anatomy and physiology laboratory equipment. Special Instructions to Applicant La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Posting Information Application Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Portfolio (PDF) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
