    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6182": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Communication Sciences and Disorders (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Assistant Professor, Communication Sciences and Disorders (Tenure Track) Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Assistant Professor, Communication Sciences and Disorders (Tenure Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (sick leave and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Position Details Position Overview Position Title Assistant Professor, Communication Sciences and Disorders (Tenure Track) Department 281950 - Communication Sciences & Disorders Appointment Term Tenure Track Position Classification Full-Time, 9 months (Faculty) Grant/Gift Funded (all or a portion)? No If Temporary or Grant Funded, Start Date and End Date Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number FA198PST Position Summary The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders ( CSD ) in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences at La Salle University invites applicants to apply for a 9-month, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The CSD Department houses both an undergraduate major in Communication Sciences and Disorders and a graduate program in speech-language pathology accredited by the Council on Academic Accreditation ( CAA ). The ideal candidate will have expertise and clinical experience in medical speech-language pathology and passion for educating and mentoring future SLPs. Essential Duties Demonstrate teaching excellence in the undergraduate, post-baccalaureate, and graduate programs. Supervise students on special projects, including independent studies and research. Meet with students at least once per semester for academic advising. Maintain regular office hours for students. Demonstrate active involvement in the CSD Department, the School of Nursing and Health Sciences, the University, and professional and/or community organizations. Secondary Responsibilities Represent the CSD department, programs, and clinical services at sponsored events Required Qualifications PhD or EdD in speech-language pathology or a related field. Candidates who are ABD and anticipate completing their degree by December 31, 2026, are encouraged to apply. Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology and eligibility for PA licensure as a speech-language pathologist. Commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and clinical supervision, and a willingness to serve our well-established, innovative programs and clinics at the University and in the broader community. Expertise in one or more of the following areas: motor-speech, feeding, swallowing, voice, and upper airway disorders. Additional experience in augmentative and alternative communication, fluency disorders, and/or bilingualism is a plus. Knowledge of and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience in the field of communication sciences and disorders or a related discipline. Knowledge and experience with course subject matter, evidence-based teaching and learning practices for in-person and virtual platforms, and student learning assessment and instruction within the discipline. Familiarity with the principles of clinical education and supervision, as well as experience supervising graduate student clinicians. Experience teaching in-person, online, and/or in hybrid formats. Experience with learning management systems such as Canvas and content tools such as PowerPoint, etc. Candidates should have excellent communication skills and a student-inspired approach to teaching for educational excellence, equity, advocacy, and service to diverse students and communities. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours The position will require teaching courses in the evenings a few nights a week and periodically attending university events on the weekend. Special Instructions to Applicant La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (sick leave and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Posting Information Application Open Date 04/17/2026 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcript(s) Optional Documents Statement of Research Interests Teaching Evaluations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the status of your doctorate (at the time of this application)? I have completed my doctorate I am ABD and expect to finish my doctorate by the start of this appointment I am ABD and don't expect to finish my doctorate by the start of this appointment I am working on it, but am not yet ABD I have not started working on my doctorate * Briefly list your area(s) of research or teaching expertise. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have previous teaching experience in higher education? Yes No * Are you familiar with varied instructional delivery methods including online and hybrid formats? Yes No * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6160": {
      "title": "Chair and Associate Professor, Graduate Nursing (Non-Tenure Track)",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Chair and Associate Professor, Graduate Nursing (Non-Tenure Track) Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Chair and Associate Professor, Graduate Nursing (Non-Tenure Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of the application you will be required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement beneﬁts, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition beneﬁts such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Position Details Position Overview Position Title Chair and Associate Professor, Graduate Nursing (Non-Tenure Track) Department 281400 - MS Nursing Appointment Term Non-Tenure Track Position Classification Full-Time, 9 months (Faculty) Grant/Gift Funded (all or a portion)? No If Temporary or Grant Funded, Start Date and End Date Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number FA195PST Position Summary The Department of Nursing within the School of Nursing and Health Sciences invites applications for a Chair of the Graduate Nursing Program who will serve as a full-time, benefits-eligible, non-tenure-track faculty member at a rank of Assistant or Associate. This is a 9-month faculty appointment accompanied by a 12-month secondary administrative appointment as Chair. The faculty and Chair roles are interdependent and must be held concurrently; continuation in each role is contingent upon service in the other. * Rank (Assistant or Associate) will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Essential Duties The successful candidate will be expected to assume the position of Chair and perform teaching responsibilities within the graduate program. Provide strategic leadership and operational oversight for graduate nursing programs to ensure academic excellence and student success. Ensure full compliance with CCNE accreditation standards and PA BON regulations, lead preparation and submission of all required reports. Oversee curriculum design, implementation, and continuous improvement aligned with accreditation standards and evolving healthcare needs. Direct the launch and accreditation of new post-licensure programs. Recruit, mentor, and evaluate faculty to foster a collaborative, growth-oriented environment. Monitor and improve student outcomes including retention, graduation rates, and national certification exam pass rates. Teach graduate nursing courses as assigned. Work closely with the Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences ( SONHS ) as an integral part of a dedicated team of chairs and program directors. Represent the department on University committees and initiatives. Establish and maintain relationships with healthcare organizations and community partners to support clinical placements and professional opportunities for students. Secondary Responsibilities Other related duties as assigned by the Dean of SONHS . Required Qualifications Doctoral degree in nursing or an appropriate discipline from an accredited institution. Current registered nurse (RN) license in Pennsylvania or multistate license. Current certified registered nurse practitioner ( CRNP ) licensure in Pennsylvania. Current national certification as a nurse practitioner, FNP preferred. A minimum of five years of recent classroom and clinical experience. Program oversight and/or leadership experience in higher education. Excellent verbal and written communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills. Evidence of scholarship, other than doctoral dissertation, which may be demonstrated by contributions to the professional literature, presentations at national, state, or local meetings and/or grantsmanship. Participation in School and/or University Committees. Participation in professional organizations at local, state or national levels. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience as a Chair or Director. Prior experience with program and curriculum development. Experience working with nursing accrediting and licensing bodies. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours The Chair is required to be available on a 12-month basis. Some evening and weekend work will be required at times, including for student recruitment events and other departmental activities. Special Instructions to Applicant As part of the application you will be required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement beneﬁts, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition beneﬁts such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Posting Information Application Open Date 03/26/2026 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in a related position? None Less than 3 years 3-5 years 6-8 years More than 8 years * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6434": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Mathematics",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Mathematics Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Mathematics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Mathematics Department 215410 - Math, Computer Science, & Physics Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0197P Position Summary The Department of Mathematics and Computer Science at La Salle University invites applications for adjunct mathematics faculty. Areas of need typically include but are not limited to college algebra, quantitative literacy, business calculus, and Calculus I. Essential Duties Responsible for all aspects of instruction for the course. Required Qualifications A master’s degree in mathematics or a related field. Knowledge of and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations Transcript(s) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * Please indicate your availability for day or evening course offerings. Only day Only evening Flexible, with notice Only weekend seminar format * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
