    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6408": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Religion and Theology",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Religion and Theology Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Religion and Theology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Religion and Theology Department 212310 - Religion and Theology Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0195P Position Summary La Salle University’s Religion & Theology program in the Department of Humanity & Society has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach on an “as needed” basis. In particular, we are looking for instructors for our courses in eastern religions ( REL 231 Buddhism in Asia and Beyond, REL 238 Tibetan Buddhism, REL 271 Yoga, Dharma, and Devotion, REL 355 Meditation and Mindfulness). Instructors must be available to teach in person during the daytime. For more information about the Religion & Theology program, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/programs/religion/. Essential Duties • Teach assigned course(s). • Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. • Provide timely grading and feedback to students. • Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications • Master’s degree in Religion or Religious Studies or closely related field. • Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications • Ph.D. in Religion or Religious Studies. • Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. • Willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours • Classes are offered in person during the day. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 09/13/2026 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of 