    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6362": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Economics",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Economics Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Economics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Economics Department 211410 - Economics Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0166P Position Summary La Salle University’s Economics department has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach a variety of courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. There may be a need for an individual to teach Sports Economics. Courses generally taught by adjunct faculty may include: Introduction to Macroeconomics, Labor Economics, Political Economics, and International Economics. These courses are generally offered in person, in both the daytime/evenings. For more information about the Department of Economics, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/programs/economics/. Essential Duties • Prepare meaningful lectures and class activities for the full duration of the published class time for each class period according to academic calendar. • Create a syllabus that meets the Provost’s Syllabus Checklist requirements. • Create assessment activities that support the stated learning outcomes for the course. • Address student questions in a timely and helpful manner. • Use Canvas and other technology to enhance student learning. • Support and follow University policies and procedures. • Attend faculty meetings. • Submit grades and materials for assessment projects on or before stated deadlines. • Communicate student concerns with personnel in the program. Required Qualifications • Master’s degree in Economics or closely related field. • Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications • Ph.D. in field. • Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. • Willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. * Knowledge in Sports Economics, Entertainment Industry Economics, Healthcare Economics or Labor Economics Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours • Some classes offered may be in the evenings, on weekends, or online. Special Instructions to Applicant La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 04/19/2024 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6356": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which UNDERGRADUATE ADJUNCT INSTRUCTORS will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Here is the Undergraduate program webpage: https://www.lasalle.edu/catalog/undergraduate/school-of-arts-and-sciences/department-of-psychology/psychology/#ftoc-program-description There are OTHER ADS for specific pools for teaching in the MASTERS and DOCTORAL programs. Please also see and apply through those ads if you are also interested in graduate level teaching. We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should a review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology Department 215510 - Psychology Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0114P Position Summary La Salle University’s Psychology department has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach a variety of courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. These courses are generally offered in person during the day and evening. Occasionally, an online course will become available. La Salle University is a Lasallian Catholic university committed to the principle that all knowledge is practical and empowering, filled with the capacity to transform lives. Anchored in the living tradition of the Brothers of the Christian Schools and in association with a diverse and inclusive learning community, our mission is to educate the whole person by fostering a rigorous free search for truth. La Salle, in affirming the value of both liberal arts and professional studies, prepares students for the lifelong pursuit and exploration of wisdom, knowledge, and faith that lead to engaged and fulfilling lives marked by a commitment to the common good. The University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. We welcome candidates whose experience in research, teaching, and service has prepared them to contribute to our department’s commitment to building a culturally diverse intellectual community. For more information about the Psychology department, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/psychology . Essential Duties Teach assigned course(s). Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. Provide timely grading and feedback to students. Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications Required of instructors in ALL programs: Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Multicultural competence and training. Undergraduate Program: Master’s degree (M.A.) or above in psychology or in a closely related field. Professional Clinical Counseling Master’s Program: M.A. or Ph.D. Doctorate in Counselor Education & Supervision (preferably from a CACREP accredited program and with a mental health counseling specialty), Psychology, or a closely related area, depending on the course. Marriage and Family Therapy or Couple and Family Therapy Master’s Program: M.A. or Ph.D. in Marriage & Family Therapy, Couple & Family Therapy (preferably from a COAMFTE -accredited program), Psychology, or a closely related area depending on the course. License-eligible as an LMFT in the state of Pennsylvania for certain courses. Doctoral Psy.D. in Clinical Psychology Program: Doctoral degree in psychology in a relevant area. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in psychology or a closely related field. Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. Willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Must be able to teach in-person on La Salle’s main campus in Philadelphia, PA. Some courses are held during the evening. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which UNDERGRADUATE ADJUNCT INSTRUCTORS will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Here is the Undergraduate program webpage: https://www.lasalle.edu/catalog/undergraduate/school-of-arts-and-sciences/department-of-psychology/psychology/#ftoc-program-description There are OTHER ADS for specific pools for teaching in the MASTERS and DOCTORAL programs. Please also see and apply through those ads if you are also interested in graduate level teaching. We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should a review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 05/03/2022 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations Transcript(s) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you able to teach in-person 1-2 days per week on La Salle's Main Campus in Philadelphia, PA? Yes No * Are you able to teach 3 days a week on La Salle University's Main Campus in Philadelphia? Yes No * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) * What is the highest degree that you hold? High School Diploma BA or BS degree (college degree) Master's degree in Psychology or a related field Doctorate in a field related to psychology or counseling Doctorate in Psychology Doctorate in Counselor Education, Mental Health Counseling, or related (CACREP accredited) Doctorate in Marriage and Family, Couples Therapy, or related (COAMFT accredited) Other * If your answer to the above questions was \"other,\" please explain. (Open Ended Question) * The next question will ask you to indicate which undergraduate courses you are both qualified and willing to teach. The descriptions of these courses can be found on the following webpage. You may want to open it in a separate window before answering the next question. https://www.lasalle.edu/catalog/undergraduate/school-of-arts-and-sciences/department-of-psychology/psychology/#ftoc-course-descriptions If you would also like to be considered for graduate teaching, please see the MA and PsyD Program ads. Was this information helpful helpful to you? Yes No * Which of the following undergraduate courses are you qualified and willing to teach? PSY 155 Introduction to Psychology PSY 210 Developmental Psychology PSY 215 Adult Development and Aging PSY 220 Psychopathology PSY 225 Social Psychology PSY 230 Industrial and Business Psychology PSY 242 Introduction to Language (cross-listed with SLH 100) PSY 245 Forensic Psychology PSY 250 Human Sexuality PSY 255 Psychology of Women PSY 260 Sports Psychology PSY 310 Statistics I PSY 311 Statistics II PSY 330 Research Design I PSY 331 Research Design II PSY 340 Psychological Assessment PSY 342 Language Development (cross-listed with SLH 203) PSY 350 Counseling Theories and Principles PSY 360 Health Psychology PSY 405 Emotions PSY 410 Theories of Learning PSY 415 Cognitive Psychology PSY 420 Biological Psychology PSY 425 Theories of Personality PSY 430 History and Systems of Psychology * What courses have you taught before and at what level? Please list them. (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
