      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Biology, Biostatistics, Genomics",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Instructor, Biology, Biostatistics, Genomics Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Instructor, Biology, Biostatistics, Genomics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In your cover letter, please describe your teaching experience and/or qualifications for teaching biostatistics and/or genomics. In your application, please provide 3 professional references with contact information. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Instructor, Biology, Biostatistics, Genomics Department 215110 - Biology and Integrated Science, Bus & Tech Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0186P Position Summary La Salle University’s Natural Sciences Department has need for a highly qualified adjunct instructor to teach biostatistics and phage genomics courses for Biology majors. These courses are currently scheduled in-person and in the daytime. For more information about the Biology department, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/biology. Essential Duties Teach assigned course(s). Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. Provide timely grading and feedback to students. Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications Master’s or PhD degree in a biology or related field. For teaching biostatistics, proficiency in the R and R Studio software environments. For teaching phage genomics, general comfort with using common genomics software tools. Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching biology courses at the college-level. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours The job requires the ability to teach lecture sections in a computer lab. The job requires movement around the classroom. Special Instructions to Applicant In your cover letter, please describe your teaching experience and/or qualifications for teaching biostatistics and/or genomics. In your application, please provide 3 professional references with contact information. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position 