    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/5623": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Nurse Anesthesia Faculty",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Nurse Anesthesia Faculty Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Nurse Anesthesia Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Nurse Anesthesia Faculty Department 281400 - MS Nursing Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0178P Position Summary The La Salle University Graduate Nursing Program is seeking an adjunct instructor to teach on campus, for various didactic courses including but not limited to courses in the Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner, Family Nurse Practitioner, and Adult Gerontology Nurse Practitioner, and Doctor of Nursing Practice starting in the Fall 2025 semester and beyond Essential Duties Teaches students at a high level of expertise. Complies with the syllabus of assigned courses, following the directives of the Director. Contributes to the revisions of syllabi for assigned course in consultation with faculty and Director of the program. Attends faculty orientation programs and meetings with course coordinators. Creates exams and grades assignments for the course(s) as specified by the course syllabus. Follows guidelines for course and clinical sections as formulated and communicated by course faculty coordinating each course. Directs students on course assignments as specified in syllabi and in consultation with faculty coordinating each course. Provides email to students and clinical faculty. Uses University mail exclusively and frequently for communicating course information with students and program information with Director of the program. Uses the La Salle Portal to access information about courses and programs. In consultation with the Director and staff, provides instruction for students. Provides students information about their performance on tests, assignments, and evaluations. Shares plans with students on improving performance. Required Qualifications MSN Expertise in subject matter Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching in higher education environment preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Day and evening hours Special Instructions to Applicant La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 03/24/2025 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in a related position? None Less than 3 years 3-5 years 6-8 years More than 8 years * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/5621": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Nurse Anesthesia",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Nurse Anesthesia Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Nurse Anesthesia Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Nurse Anesthesia Department 231100 - Nursing Undergraduate Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0177P Position Summary The La Salle University Nurse Anesthesia Program is seeking an adjunct instructor to teach in the post- BSN to DNP program by participation in didactic and clinical curriculum, recruitment, and evaluation with the support of Nurse Anesthesia Program Director and Assistant Program Director. . Essential Duties Teaches students at a high level of expertise. Complies with the syllabus of assigned courses, following the directives of the Chair. Attends immersion day. Contributes to the revisions of syllabi for assigned course in consultation with faculty and Chair of Undergraduate program. Attends faculty orientation programs and meetings with course coordinators. Creates exams and grades assignments for the course(s) as specified by the course syllabus. Follows guidelines for course and clinical sections as formulated and communicated by course faculty coordinating each course. Directs students on course assignments as specified in syllabi and in consultation with faculty coordinating each course. Provides email to students and clinical faculty. Uses University mail exclusively and frequently for communicating course information with students and program information with Chair of Undergraduate program. Uses the La Salle Portal to access information about courses and programs. In consultation with the Chair and staff, provides remedial instruction for students. Provides students information about their performance on tests, assignments, and evaluations. Shares plans with students on improving performance. Required Qualifications Five or more years of clinical experience in the Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist ( CRNA ) role. (Standard B-9a) Pre-licensure master’s or doctoral degree with a Nurse Anesthesia major from a regionally accredited institution and nationally accredited nurse anesthesia program (or equivalent) with graduate preparation in the basic and clinical sciences relevant to nurse anesthesia practice. (Standard B-9b) Demonstrated record of professional and clinical experience, instruction (teaching), curriculum, evaluation development, and scholarship. (Standard B-9c) Knowledge of current CRNA practice and related professional issues (standard B-9d) Current knowledge of institutional and programmatic accreditation requirements for nurse anesthesia educational programs (Standard B-9e) Earned doctorate preferred in nursing or related field from an institution of higher education that was accredited by an agency officially recognized by the US Secretary of Education to accredit institutions at the time the degree was conferred. (Standard B-10) A current unencumbered license to practice as a registered professional nurse (RN) and/or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse ( APRN ) in Pennsylvania. (Standard B-11) Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist ( CRNA ) licensure by the NBCRNA . (Standard B-12) Demonstrated experience working in and fostering a diverse faculty, staff, and student environment. Knowledge of and commitment to the mission of La Salle University and diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching in higher education environment preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours This position typically works during La Salle business hours, 8:30am-4:30pm. Weekend or evening work may be required in certain situations. Special Instructions to Applicant La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 03/24/2025 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in a related position? None Less than 3 years 3-5 years 6-8 years More than 8 years * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - 