    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/5476": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Biology",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Biology Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In your cover letter, please describe your microbiology teaching experience and/or qualifications for teaching microbiology. In the letter, please provide 2 professional references with contact information. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Biology Department 215110 - Biology and Integrated Science, Bus & Tech Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0171P Position Summary La Salle University’s Natural Sciences department has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach introductory microbiology lecture and laboratory classes for first-year nursing majors and pre-health majors. These courses are generally offered in person, in the daytime or evenings. For more information about the Biology department, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/biology Essential Duties • Teach assigned course(s). • Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. • Provide timely grading and feedback to students. • Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications Master’s or PhD degree in a biology, microbiology, or related field. A Master’s or terminal degree in related degree in a field related to microbiology (MD, DO, etc) will also be considered. Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Experience or desire for teaching introductory biology and/or microbiology courses, particularly at the college-level. Knowledge or experience teaching anatomy and physiology laboratory courses. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours The job requires the ability to teach lecture or lab sections of microbiology. The job requires movement around the classroom or laboratory. It may be necessary for the position to teach an evening class of microbiology. Special Instructions to Applicant In your cover letter, please describe your microbiology teaching experience and/or qualifications for teaching microbiology. In the letter, please provide 2 professional references with contact information. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date Application Close Date Application Open To Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Teaching Evaluations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/5363": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Biology",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Biology Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In your cover letter, please describe your anatomy and physiology teaching experience and/or qualifications for teaching anatomy and physiology. In the letter, please provide 2 professional references with contact information.. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Biology Department 215110 - Biology and Integrated Science, Bus & Tech Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0170P Position Summary La Salle University’s Natural SciencesDdepartment has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach Anatomy and Physiology lecture and laboratory classes. These courses are generally offered in person, in the daytime or evenings. For more information about the Chemistry department, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/chemistry Essential Duties • Teach assigned course(s). • Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. • Provide timely grading and feedback to students. • Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications Master’s or PhD degree in a biology, anatomy, physiology or related field. A Master’s or terminal degree in related degree in a field related to anatomy/physiology (MD, DO, DPt, etc) will also be considered. Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Experience or desire for teaching biology and/or anatomy and physiology courses, particularly at the college-level. Knowledge or experience teaching anatomy and physiology laboratory courses. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours The job requires the ability to teach lecture or lab sections of A&P. The job requires movement around the classroom or laboratory, and possibly lifting heavy objects such as anatomy models. It may be necessary for the position to teach an evening class of A&P. Special Instructions to Applicant In your cover letter, please describe your anatomy and physiology teaching experience and/or qualifications for teaching anatomy and physiology. In the letter, please provide 2 professional references with contact information.. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 07/07/2024 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
