    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4992": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Nursing Pediatrics Didactic Instructorl",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Nursing Pediatrics Didactic Instructorl Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Nursing Pediatrics Didactic Instructorl Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Nursing Pediatrics Didactic Instructorl Department 231100 - Nursing Undergraduate Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0161P Position Summary The La Salle University Undergraduate Nursing Program is seeking an adjunct instructor to teach an on campus, NUR 335: Family Nursing: Childrearing Families course scheduled during the Summer 2024 Session; Tuesdays, 6 pm – 8 pm, starting 5/20/24 – 8/8/24. Essential Duties Teaches students at a high level of expertise. Complies with the syllabus of assigned courses, following the directives of the Chair. Attends immersion day. Contributes to the revisions of syllabi for assigned course in consultation with faculty and Chair of Undergraduate program. Attends faculty orientation programs and meetings with course coordinators. Creates exams and grades assignments for the course(s) as specified by the course syllabus. Follows guidelines for course and clinical sections as formulated and communicated by course faculty coordinating each course. Directs students on course assignments as specified in syllabi and in consultation with faculty coordinating each course. Provides email to students and clinical faculty. Uses University mail exclusively and frequently for communicating course information with students and program information with Chair of Undergraduate program. Uses the La Salle Portal to access information about courses and programs. In consultation with the Chair and staff, provides remedial instruction for students. Provides students information about their performance on tests, assignments, and evaluations. Shares plans with students on improving performance. Required Qualifications MSN Expertise in pediatric nursing Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching in higher education environment preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Tuesdays, 6 pm – 8 pm, starting 5/20/24 – 8/8/24. Special Instructions to Applicant La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 02/07/2024 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in a related position? None Less than 3 years 3-5 years 6-8 years More than 8 years * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * How did you 