    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4769": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty for Psychopharmacology - PsyD Program in Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty for Psychopharmacology - PsyD Program in Clinical Psychology Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty for Psychopharmacology - PsyD Program in Clinical Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a new posting to hire an adjunct instructor for our psychopharmacology course (PSY 750). This position requires a graduate degree in psychology or a closely related field. Here is the webpage for the Psy.D. Program in Clinical Psychology: https://www.lasalle.edu/doctor-of-psychology/ There are also other pooled position ads for teaching in the undergraduate and masters programs. Please see and apply for those positions if you are interested. We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty for Psychopharmacology - PsyD Program in Clinical Psychology Department 281560 - Doctoral Psychology Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0149P Position Summary La Salle University’s Psy.D. Program in Clinical Psychology has a need for a highly qualified adjunct faculty person to teach our Psychopharmacology Course. This course may be taught in-person or remote with specific meeting times (synchronous). For more information about the Psy.D. Program, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/doctor-of-psychology/. We welcome candidates whose experience in research, teaching, and service has prepared them to contribute to our department’s commitment to evidence-based practice and building a culturally diverse intellectual community. For more information about the Psychology department, please visit www.lasalle.edu/psychology. La Salle University is a Lasallian Catholic university committed to the principle that all knowledge is practical and empowering, filled with the capacity to transform lives. Anchored in the living tradition of the Brothers of the Christian Schools and in association with a diverse and inclusive learning community, our mission is to educate the whole person by fostering a rigorous free search for truth. La Salle, in affirming the value of both liberal arts and professional studies, prepares students for the lifelong pursuit and exploration of wisdom, knowledge, and faith that lead to engaged and fulfilling lives marked by a commitment to the common good. The University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Essential Duties Teach assigned course(s). Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. Provide timely grading and feedback to students. Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications Graduate degree in Psychology or closely related field. Multicultural competence and training. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. Willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Some courses are held during the evening. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a new posting to hire an adjunct instructor for our psychopharmacology course ( PSY 750). This position requires a graduate degree in psychology or a closely related field. Here is the webpage for the Psy.D. Program in Clinical Psychology: https://www.lasalle.edu/doctor-of-psychology/ There are also other pooled position ads for teaching in the undergraduate and masters programs. Please see and apply for those positions if you are interested. We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 07/25/2023 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Teaching Evaluations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * What courses have you taught before at the graduate school level? Please list them. (Open Ended Question) * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
