      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology, Online Biopsychology Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology, Online Biopsychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a course specific position announcement for an online section of Biopsychology at the undergraduate level for Fall 2023 . If you are interested in other teaching opportunities in Psychology, please see the general Psychology Undergraduate position announcement. Here is the Undergraduate program webpage: https://www.lasalle.edu/catalog/undergraduate/school-of-arts-and-sciences/department-of-psychology/psychology/#ftoc-program-description There are OTHER ADS for specific pools for teaching in the MASTERS and DOCTORAL programs. Please also see and apply through those ads if you are also interested in graduate level teaching. We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should a review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology, Online Biopsychology Department 215510 - Psychology Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0147P Position Summary La Salle University’s Psychology department has a need for an instructor for an undergraduate section of Biopsychology in an online format. La Salle University is a Lasallian Catholic university committed to the principle that all knowledge is practical and empowering, filled with the capacity to transform lives. Anchored in the living tradition of the Brothers of the Christian Schools and in association with a diverse and inclusive learning community, our mission is to educate the whole person by fostering a rigorous free search for truth. La Salle, in affirming the value of both liberal arts and professional studies, prepares students for the lifelong pursuit and exploration of wisdom, knowledge, and faith that lead to engaged and fulfilling lives marked by a commitment to the common good. The University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. We welcome candidates whose experience in research, teaching, and service has prepared them to contribute to our department’s commitment to building a culturally diverse intellectual community. For more information about the Psychology department, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/psychology . Essential Duties Teach assigned course(s). Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. Provide timely grading and feedback to students. Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications Required of instructors in ALL programs: Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Multicultural competence and training. Undergraduate Program: Master’s degree (M.A.) or above in psychology or in a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in psychology or a closely related field. Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. Specialized knowledge of Biopsychology Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Special Instructions to Applicant This is a course specific position announcement for an online section of Biopsychology at the undergraduate level for Fall 2023 . If you are interested in other teaching opportunities in Psychology, please see the general Psychology Undergraduate position announcement. Here is the Undergraduate program webpage: https://www.lasalle.edu/catalog/undergraduate/school-of-arts-and-sciences/department-of-psychology/psychology/#ftoc-program-description There are OTHER ADS for specific pools for teaching in the MASTERS and DOCTORAL programs. Please also see and apply through those ads if you are also interested in graduate level teaching. We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should a review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 07/14/2023 Application Close Date 05/31/2024 Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations Transcript(s) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest degree that you hold? High School Diploma BA or BS degree (college degree) Master's degree in Psychology or a related field Doctorate in a field related to psychology or counseling Doctorate in Psychology Doctorate in Counselor Education, Mental Health Counseling, or related (CACREP accredited) Doctorate in Marriage and Family, Couples Therapy, or related (COAMFT accredited) Other * If your answer to the above questions was \"other,\" please explain. (Open Ended Question) * What courses have you taught before and at what level? Please list them. (Open Ended Question) * What are your qualifications for teaching an undergraduate, online course in Biopsychology? (Open Ended Question) * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
