    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4711": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Communication Sciences and Disorders",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Communication Sciences and Disorders Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Communication Sciences and Disorders Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Communication Sciences and Disorders Department 281950 - Communication Sciences & Disorders Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0146P Position Summary La Salle University’s Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders, with a CAA -accredited MS program in Speech-Language Pathology, seeks an adjunct professor. Adjunct teaching opportunities may include undergraduate and graduate courses across the curriculum and graduate student clinical supervision. Given our emphasis on teaching, collaboration, and clinical training, candidates will have an understanding of evidence-based practice, community–based learning, team approaches to service delivery, and integration of teaching and clinical practice. At this time, we have a specific opening for a clinical supervisor in the La Salle University Speech-Language-Hearing Community Clinics ( LSU - SLHCC ) to be taught in Fall 2023. Essential Duties • Provide guidance and clinical supervision for approximately 7 first-year graduate students, each treating one client in the LSU - SLHCC . • Use Learning Management System (Canvas) to post course content and grades. • Maintains availability to meet with students concerning the course. • Be present on campus for ½ day per week for 16 weeks to supervise and meet with students. Required Qualifications • Earned Master’s degree (speech-language pathology) • Must have CCC - SLP (Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology) granted by the American-Speech-Language-Hearing Association ( ASHA ) • Must hold PA licensure as a speech-language pathologist or audiologist • Must have completed a minimum of two years of practice experience post-certification ( CCC - SLP ) • Must have earned (or are willing to earn) at least two hours of professional development post-certification (one-time requirement) in the area of supervision and/or clinical instruction • Knowledge of and commitment to the mission of La Salle University Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours • Evening and weekend work may be necessary when teaching graduate courses. • Some clinical courses require travel to external sites. Special Instructions to Applicant La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 06/05/2023 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
