    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4684": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Public Health - LEAP Program",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Public Health - LEAP Program Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Public Health - LEAP Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Public Health - LEAP Program Department 281960 - Public Health Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0117P Position Summary The La Salle University Public Health Program is seeking to hire instructors for online synchronous Public Health 101 courses with High School Students enrolled as part of the dual enrollment program. Most sections will run in the morning, at either 8:00am – 8:50am EST or 9:00am – 9:45am EST on Monday, Wednesday and Friday or Monday, Tuesday and Thursday. Essential Duties 1. Teaches students at a high level of expertise. 2. Complies with the La Salle syllabus template and accessibility requirements, contributing revisions as needed. 3. Attends faculty orientation meetings with course coordinators prior to the start of the semester. 4. Attends class on the dates and for the hours designated for the course(s). 5. Evaluates course performance of students using course rubrics and/or other methods of evaluation. 6. Grades assignments for the course(s) as specified by the course syllabus. 7. Directs students on course assignments as specified in syllabi 8. Utilizes La Salle University email, the La Salle Portal, and Canvas course software to communicate course information with students and program information. 9. Provides remedial instruction for students, under the guidance of the Program Director or Coordinator. 10. Provides academic support for students in need of improving academic performance. Required Qualifications Master’s or Doctoral Degree in Public Health or related field Expertise in public health and previous teaching experience. Knowledge of and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Previous online teaching experience Previous teaching experience with high school students in dual enrollment programs Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 10/27/2022 