      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Marriage &amp; Family Therapy Master&#39;s Program",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Marriage &amp; Family Therapy Master&#39;s Program Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Marriage & Family Therapy Master's Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Marriage & Family Therapy Master's Program Department 281500 - M.A. Clinical Counsel Psychology Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0102P Position Summary La Salle University’s Marriage & Family Therapy Master’s Program has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach a variety of courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. These courses are typically offered in person during the late afternoon and evening on La Salle’s Main Campus in Philadelphia, PA. For more information about the Marriage & Family Therapy Master’s Program, please visit www.lasalle.edu/counseling-family-therapy/. Essential Duties • Teach assigned course(s). • Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. • Provide timely grading and feedback to students. • Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications • Master’s degree in marriage & family therapy or a related field. Individuals with degrees in counseling are encouraged to apply to La Salle’s M.A. Program in Professional Clinical Counseling. • Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications • Previous experience teaching at a collegiate level. • Clinical experience in the mental health field. • Experience as a clinical supervisor. • Willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours • Must be able to teach in-person on La Salle’s Main Campus in Philadelphia, PA or online. • Able to teach late afternoons/evenings. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 06/28/2021 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have previous teaching experience in higher education? Yes No Do you have previous experience teaching online? Yes No Are you available to teach online courses, courses offered on campus, or both? Online On Campus Both Do you have a Master's degree in counseling or a related field at the time of this application? Yes No How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Do you have a degree in marriage & family therapy at the time of this application? (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
