    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4663": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Management &amp; Leadership, LEAP course on Innovation and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Management &amp; Leadership, LEAP course on Innovation and Entrepreneurship Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Management & Leadership, LEAP course on Innovation and Entrepreneurship Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested parties should submit a cover letter, CV or résumé, and, if available, PDFs of course evaluations for courses recently taught. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Management & Leadership, LEAP course on Innovation and Entrepreneurship Department 221410 - Management & Leadership Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0142P Position Summary La Salle’s Early Achievement Program ( LEAP ) offers credit-bearing college-level courses to motivated students at partner high schools. The Management and Leadership Department is seeking instructors for a new course, ENT 170: Innovation and Entrepreneurship, that will be offered in Summer 2023. We are especially looking for instructors who can bring energy, creativity, enthusiasm, support, and encouragement to high school students in this experiential, project-based course. Sections will meet in-person at La Salle’s campus on Tuesday and Thursday mornings (10 AM to noon) or afternoons (1 PM to 3 PM) for six weeks, from June 20 to July 27, 2023. Students will receive additional instruction through asynchronous online activities. The course will follow a common syllabus, workbook, and structure, and a course coordinator will provide instructors with advance training and guidance. Essential Duties Attend training sessions and familiarize oneself in advance with upcoming presentation content, book materials, and student assignments Lead class meetings in a manner consistent with the structure of the course, while also being flexible in adapting to the rate of learning among students Encourage discussion, engagement, and student involvement; be creative in seeking and highlighting learning moments in class activities Support and mentor student teams Collaborate with the course coordinator, other instructors, and LEAP student mentors as needed Be available to address questions and assist students as students complete asynchronous assignments Provide timely grading and feedback to students Required Qualifications A master’s degree or higher Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Special Instructions to Applicant Interested parties should submit a cover letter, CV or résumé, and, if available, PDFs of course evaluations for courses recently taught. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 03/23/2023 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
