    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4645": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, History",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, History Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, History Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Please submit a 1-page letter of interest and a resume/c.v. with contact information for 3 references. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, History Department 211910 - History Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0136P Position Summary La Salle University’s History program has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach a variety of courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. These courses are generally offered in person, during the day, as well as online. For more information about the History program, please visit www.lasalle.edu/history Essential Duties • Teach assigned course(s). • Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. • Provide timely grading and feedback to students. • Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications • Master’s degree in History or