    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4644": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Foreign Language, Japanese",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Foreign Language, Japanese Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Foreign Language, Japanese Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Foreign Language, Japanese Department 211810 - Global Languages,Literature&Perspec and Art Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0140P Position Summary The Department of Global Languages, Literatures, and Perspectives on our main campus is seeking a part-time adjunct instructor to teach elementary Japanese courses. Essential Duties • Prepare meaningful lectures and class activities for the full duration of the published class time for each class period according to academic calendar. • Create a syllabus that meets the Provost’s Syllabus Checklist requirements. • Create assessment activities that support the stated learning outcomes for the course. • Address student questions in a timely and helpful manner. • Use Canvas and other technology to enhance student learning. • Support and follow University policies and procedures as well as those for the department. • Attend faculty meetings. • Submit grades and materials for assessment projects on or before stated deadlines. • Communicate student concerns with personnel in the department. Required Qualifications • Master’s degree in Japanese or related field. • Native or near native fluency in Japanese and English • Able to teach fall, spring or summer Preferred Qualifications • PhD in Japanese or related field. • Experience in teaching college level Japanese. • Experience using technology is a plus Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours • None Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 03/14/2023 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's