    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4636": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Art History",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Art History Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Art History Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Please submit a 1-page letter of interest and a resume/c.v. with contact information for 3 references. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Art History Department 211110 - Art Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0097P Position Summary La Salle University’s Art History program has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach a variety of courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. Courses generally taught by adjunct faculty may include: Intro to Art History, Ancient Art, Medieval Art, Renaissance Art, Baroque Art, American Art, American Architecture, and some aspect of Global Art. These courses are generally offered in person, during the day or in the evening, as well as online. For more information about the Art History program, please visit www.lasalle.edu/arthistory Essential Duties • Teach assigned course(s). • Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. • Provide timely grading and feedback to students. • Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications • Master’s degree in Art History or closely related field. • Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications • PhD in Art History or closely related field. • Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. • Willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours • Some classes offered may be in the evenings or online. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Please submit a 1-page letter of interest and a resume/c.v. with contact information for 3 references. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 10/26/2022 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Doc 1 (See Posting) Other Doc 2 (See Posting) Other Doc 3 (See Posting) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have